message: "If you use or adapt the Context Sprint method, please cite it as below."
title: "Context Sprint: Method Definition"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Robert
    given-names: Maike
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-05
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/maikerobert/context-sprint"
abstract: >-
  Context Sprint is a product development method that takes a business need
  from a meeting to production-ready interfaces, built in the company's own
  design system and technical stack, with a human approval gate between every
  step. An AI agent carries the company's full context (the Context Layer) and
  produces each artifact; people decide at every gate. Central rule: speed
  comes from context, not from the model.
keywords:
  - context sprint
  - product development
  - artificial intelligence
  - design system
  - prototyping
  - human-in-the-loop
  - methodology
